+  <p>
+    The Asynchronous Interaction Request pattern applies to any valid RESTful request the server supports, including
+    create (<code>POST</code>), update (<code>PUT</code>), and patch (<code>PATCH</code>) interactions. The initial
+    response is <code>202 Accepted</code>; when processing completes, the polling response returns a
+    <a href="bundle.html">Bundle</a> whose first entry carries the final outcome of the original interaction, including
+    the status, any <a href="operationoutcome.html">OperationOutcome</a>, and any created or modified resource location
+    or response body when applicable.
+  </p>
   <p>
     For now, these patterns are defined in the <a href="https://build.fhir.org/ig/HL7/api-incubator">API
       Incubator</a> while the details are finalised through implementation testing.
